commit 5da4ca52ad31040143d5f272a451d5dd4e2eec53
Author: Bob Singor <bob@singor.com>
Date:   Sun Oct 11 10:11:48 2026 +0300

    Forms: every fill is one change on the queue, scripts against the view

    - plugin-form: the fields mirror predicts form ops (predictFormOp), and
      every read (getSnapshot, get, getValue, listWidgets) comes from the
      view. A fill shows at once and fields stay editable while it's on its
      way; FormState.writing and the disabled-while-writing controls are gone.
    - One fill path (write/fill.ts): hold the user's ops, run the scripts
      against the view in one realm transaction, set every op inside it and
      send. setValue, setValues/importValues (one change, one recalculation),
      reset, widget activation and script/action effects all use it. Undo
      shows forms.restore of the fields as they were.
    - A fill the engine refuses runs the calculations again, outside the
      history. A hold sent before its scripts finished (an undo, another
      plugin's change) never stages stale results: the calculations run
      again against the view instead.
    - Scripting controller reads the form it's given and returns
      FormScriptResult; transaction(body) and warm(form). Name refs
      (toFieldRef) now reach their field's scripts.
    - QuickJS starts on the first field focus, and never for a form without
      field scripts; a one-time hint when a form has scripts and no realm.
    - Submit waits for the fills on their way, then reads the view.
    - plugin-actions: registerFormReader(); script worlds, widget events,
      field trees and Hide read the form plugin's view instead of
      forms.list(). The form sink answers once the effects are staged.
    - core: PredictedOp forms.restore carries widget rows; forms.restoreWidget.
    - core-acrojs: scripts read a field's display from its first widget
      (it was always 'visible', so showing a hidden field did nothing).
    - web: the text field editor keeps the typed text after blur until the
      field shows it; a value refused by validation stays typed.
      TextFieldDrafts.commitDraftText resolves { status } | null.
    - angular: controlOf follows the field without a write counter.
    - stamp: dynamic stamps write their scripts' effects to the asset copy
      inside the transaction.
    - Tests: predictions, a seeded fill interleavings suite and an undo/redo
      suite on a real engine with real scripts, realm warming. plugin-form
      dev-depends on plugin-history.
    - Changesets, API snapshots and the headless forms docs updated.

